  "claim_short": "Candidate full negative answer to the necessity question in Remark 3.8 of arXiv:1403.5368. For n=N=1, D=-i d/dx, B=I, arbitrary 1<p<q<infinity, delta=1/p-1/q, every psi in Psi_sigma^delta and every bounded holomorphic g, the family {g(D)psi(tD)} satisfies Lp-Lq off-diagonal estimates for every 0<=K<=sigma+delta. A uniform dyadic Fourier-kernel argument gives |k_t(x)| bounded by min(|x|^(delta-1),|x|^(-1-sigma));...",
